Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the required accuracy standard for the fundamental representations and warranties.\nQuestion: How precise must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 9.4 Additional Conditions to Closing. The obligations described herein are subject to the following: (a) Representations and Warranties. The representations and warranties of the Seller, as set forth in Section 8.1, shall be true and correct as of the date hereof and as of the Closing Date as if made on such date. Notwithstanding, errors that are de minimis in nature or that do not collectively have a Material Adverse Impact on the Seller's financial position are excluded from the requirement for absolute accuracy. In contrast, any representation expressly stated without qualification must be strictly observed; however, for the majority of representations, the standard applied is one of accuracy in all material respects. (Page 55)
